# ── Private key material ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backup PRIVATE key must never enter the repository. Its whole purpose
# is to live somewhere the production host cannot reach, so that a compromised
# host cannot decrypt its own offsite snapshots — committing it here would
# hand it to anyone with clone access and to every CI runner.
#
# `backup-privkey.asc` was tracked (empty) and sat waiting for someone to paste
# a key into it; one `git add -A` later it would have been in the history.
# The PUBLIC key is deliberately NOT ignored: it belongs on every backup-
# producing host and is safe to distribute.
*.asc
!backup-pubkey.gpg
backup-privkey*
*.privkey
*-private.gpg
secring.*
